% review-id: meu-barco-e-veleiro-paraiba
% review-from: holding
% review-status: pending
% review-categories: racism, context
% review-findings: The second half is a courting line about complexion: "Eu amo a cor morena / A cor morena é que me ama" (I love the brown colour; the brown colour loves me). Morena is an everyday, affectionate word in Brazil, but like the "mulata" of Sambalele it ties a love song to skin colour.
% review-suggestion: Keep it out of the published set until a Brazilian educator (and the coco reviewer the dossier names) says how classes sing it today; the tune itself is a good tonic-arpeggio study. Do not invent replacement words here.
% review-decision:
% holding-id: meu-barco-e-veleiro-paraiba
% holding-status: transcription
% holding-owner: Codex
% holding-source-check: pending
% holding-classroom-check: pending
% holding-updated: 2026-11-10
% holding-blocked: Re-read the rhythm and barlines against p. 75 (scan p. 85); compare Andrade's Paraíba and Pernambuco versions; then have a coco practitioner review function, pulse and classroom use.
% dossier-function: coco; Andrade gives a short Paraíba verse and contrasts it with a longer Pernambuco call-and-response version
% dossier-elements: 2/4; the Paraíba melody is restricted to the tonic-triad arpeggio, as Andrade explicitly notes; one short strophe
% dossier-practice: learn the four Portuguese lines unaccompanied first; do not add a generic samba or bossa groove while the coco practice has not been reviewed
% dossier-honesty: provisional transcription of Andrade's Paraíba plate only; the Pernambuco chorus and solo that follow on the page are not silently combined with it
% dossier-licence: public domain source, first published 1928; Andrade died in 1945; the BBM/USP scan is marked public domain by Wikimedia Commons and IMSLP
% dossier-respect: label the collected place and variant; do not present this four-line Paraíba version as the only form of the song or of coco
% dossier-review: a Brazilian Portuguese speaker and a musician or culture bearer familiar with coco from Paraíba before promotion
