N:HOW READ (2026-11-10): read from the BBM/USP plate at 220 dpi and enlarged crops. The source marks 2/4, one flat and "Coco", and says this Paraíba version uses only the tonic-chord arpeggio. That pitch constraint was used as a cross-check, not as permission to regularise the rhythm.
N:UNCERTAIN: exact beaming and barlines throughout, the duration of "veleiro", and the two final bars. The source prints no tempo for this short version. Keep at transcription status until a second reader checks the plate.
